owing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-17T06:40:50Z","updated_at":"2025-04-17T06:40:50Z","body":"Tested in 4.0.4 and 4.4.0.stable. The 100% opaque behavior was due to the materials roughness being set to `1.0` decreasing this lets the material be see through again. This is [documented](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.html#refraction) (from v4.2).\n>If you can't see behind the object when refraction is enabled and albedo transparency is reduced, decrease the material's Roughness value.  \n\nWith a roughness of 1.0:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ddb2fea2-7ac0-4f3d-9ee4-b26278d9b7ad)\n\nWith a roughness of 0.2:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fdfb35b6-c4e0-4e83-af23-35f4b6cd8098)\n\nWith regards to adding support for physically based IOR (Index of Refraction) compared to just Refraction, that should rather be a proposal. Also relevant #93417 and [proposal-1934](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/1934)\n\ncc @AThousandShips -- Bug triage sprint","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2811946325/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/rep